# Jupiter 2 stable device symlinks.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# /dev/ttyUSB0 and /dev/ttyUSB1 are assigned in USB enumeration order, which
# changes across reboots and whenever a device is unplugged. On this chassis the
# CP2102 (RPLidar) and the FTDI FT232H (AX-12A head servo) regularly swap:
# jupiterobot2_lidar.launch.py once hardcoded /dev/ttyUSB1 and therefore opened
# the HEAD SERVO's bus instead of the lidar. Nothing errored -- the lidar just
# sat silent while the head bus was held.
#
# Matching on VID:PID is the fix. The FTDI and CP2102 cannot be confused because
# their vendor IDs differ (0403 vs 10c4), and unlike a serial number this does
# not depend on a particular board.
#
# INSTALL
#   sudo cp 99-jupiter.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
#   sudo udevadm trigger
#   ls -l /dev/jupiter/
#
# You must unplug/replug (or trigger) for existing devices to pick up the new
# symlinks. The symlinks live in /dev/jupiter/ so they cannot collide with
# anything else.

# --- RPLidar on the Silicon Labs CP2102 (10c4:ea60) -------------------------
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="10c4", ATTRS{idProduct}=="ea60", \
  SYMLINK+="jupiter/lidar", MODE="0666", GROUP="dialout"

# --- AX-12A head servo on the FTDI FT232H (0403:6014) -----------------------
# 6014 is the FT232H in its default configuration; if yours enumerates as a
# different FTDI product id, copy the value from `lsusb` and adjust here.
#
# latency_timer=1 is a MAJOR performance fix, not a tweak. The FTDI driver
# batches received bytes and only hands them to the tty after
# latency_timer milliseconds. Default is 16 ms, which means EVERY serial
# transaction costs 16 ms regardless of baud rate -- the AX-12 itself answers in
# 0.5 ms (measured). At 16 ms a read cycle of 5 registers took 96 ms and
# head_node could only reach 10 Hz while configured for 20 Hz. Setting it to 1
# removes that floor.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0403", ATTRS{idProduct}=="6014", \
  SYMLINK+="jupiter/head", MODE="0666", GROUP="dialout", \
  ATTR{device/latency_timer}="1"

# --- SO-100 arm on the CH340 (1a86:55d3) ------------------------------------
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="55d3", \
  SYMLINK+="jupiter/arm", MODE="0666", GROUP="dialout"

# --- ROBOTIS OpenCR base (0483:5740, STM32 CDC) -----------------------------
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0483", ATTRS{idProduct}=="5740", \
  SYMLINK+="jupiter/base", MODE="0666", GROUP="dialout"
